@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il27-tax-years`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 39B — "זיכוי בעד שירות מילואים כלוחם", the credit for reserve service as a fighter. Row IL-27.
-- Source lines 1619-1629.
--
-- Credit points in a tax year for an individual who served reserve service as a fighter in the previous tax year: three quarters of
-- a point for 20 days or more, and a quarter of a point more for each further five days, to a total of 4 points (paragraphs (1) and
-- (2)). Between and after them the consolidation prints lines marked "temporary provision in the years 2026 and 2027": half a point for
-- 30 to 39 days, three quarters for 40 to 49, one point for 50 or more, and a quarter more for each further five days beyond 50, to 4.
--
-- TWO THINGS THE SOURCES DO NOT GIVE.
-- 1. The commencement of s 39B. It was added by a Law of 5786 (the heading's amendment list ends at תשפ״ו) which is not in the source
--    bundle (the Economic Efficiency Law of 5786, Sefer HaChukim 3511, which is, does not touch s 39B). The section is answered
--    here only for tax years from 2026, the first year of the temporary provision; an earlier tax year is refused by name:
--    "needs a source".
-- 2. How the temporary lines relate to (1) and (2). They are less generous than (1) and (2) at every number of days, so they do not
--    add to them, and (1) and (2) are not marked as ending. Fork F2: the temporary provision replaces (1) and (2) in tax years 2026
--    and 2027; or (1) and (2) govern throughout. RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): one named switch, default declined where the
--    readings differ (which, from 20 days of service, is every case), both readings kept by name and tested. "In the years 2026 and
--    2027" is read as the tax years, since the section speaks "לשנת המס" (assumed, not ruled; NOTES.md A3).
--
-- DAYS. "For each five additional days" is read as each complete block of five days (NOTES.md A4). "Fighter" and "reserve service"
-- are defined by two Laws not in the source bundle; the days of reserve service as a fighter are a fact the caller states.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 39B — credit for reserve service as a fighter`

-- src:1620 | (א) בחישוב המס לשנת המס של יחיד ששירת שירות מילואים כלוחם בשנת המס שקדמה לה (להלן – שנת המס הקודמת), יובאו בחשבון נקודות זיכוי כמפורט להלן:
-- src:1621 | (1) 3 ⁄ 4 נקודת זיכוי – אם שירת שירות מילואים כלוחם 20 ימים ומעלה בשנת המס הקודמת;
-- src:1622 | [note: (הוראת שעה בשנים 2026 ו־2027):] 1 ⁄ 2 נקודת זיכוי – אם שירת שירות מילואים כלוחם בין 30 ל־39 ימים בשנת המס הקודמת;
-- src:1623 | (2) תוספת 1 ⁄ 4 נקודת זיכוי בעד כל חמישה ימים נוספים ששירת שירות מילואים כלוחם מעבר ל־20 הימים האמורים בפסקה (1), ובלבד שסך נקודות הזיכוי לפי סעיף זה לא יעלה על 4 נקודות זיכוי;
-- src:1624 | [note: (הוראת שעה בשנים 2026 ו־2027):] 3 ⁄ 4 נקודת זיכוי – אם שירת שירות מילואים כלוחם בין 40 ל־49 ימים בשנת המס הקודמת;
-- src:1625 | (3) [note: (הוראת שעה בשנים 2026 ו־2027):] נקודת זיכוי אחת – אם שירת שירות מילואים כלוחם 50 ימים ומעלה בשנת המס הקודמת;
-- src:1626 | (4) [note: (הוראת שעה בשנים 2026 ו־2027):] תוספת 1 ⁄ 4 נקודת זיכוי בעד כל חמישה ימים נוספים ששירת שירות מילואים כלוחם מעבר ל־50 הימים האמורים בפסקה (3), ובלבד שסך נקודות הזיכוי לפי סעיף זה לא יעלה על 4 נקודות זיכוי.
-- src:1627 | (ב) בסעיף זה –
-- src:1628 | ”לוחם“ – לפי פקודות הצבא כהגדרתן בחוק השיפוט הצבאי, התשט״ו–1955;
-- src:1629 | ”שירות מילואים“ – כהגדרתו בחוק שירות המילואים, התשס״ח–2008.

§§ `Paragraphs (1) and (2)`

-- (1): three quarters of a point for 20 days or more. (2): a quarter more for each five days beyond the 20, to 4 points in all.
@ref ITO s 39B(a)(1), (2), lines 1621, 1623
GIVEN `the days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 39B(a)(1), (2) — the points for days of service` `the days` MEANS
    IF   `the days` LESS THAN 20
    THEN 0
    ELSE min 4 (3/4 PLUS 1/4 TIMES FLOOR ((`the days` MINUS 20) DIVIDED BY 5))

§§ `The temporary provision for the tax years 2026 and 2027`

@ref ITO s 39B(a), the lines marked as a temporary provision, lines 1622, 1624-1626
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the temporary provision of section 39B says nothing of 20 to 29 days of service` MEANS
    REFUSE "the temporary provision of section 39B says nothing of 20 to 29 days of service"

@ref ITO s 39B(a), the lines marked as a temporary provision, lines 1622, 1624-1626
GIVEN `the days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 39B(a) temporary provision — the points for days of service` `the days` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the days` LESS THAN 20 THEN 0
        IF `the days` LESS THAN 30 THEN `the temporary provision of section 39B says nothing of 20 to 29 days of service`
        IF `the days` LESS THAN 40 THEN 1/2
        IF `the days` LESS THAN 50 THEN 3/4
        OTHERWISE min 4 (1 PLUS 1/4 TIMES FLOOR ((`the days` MINUS 50) DIVIDED BY 5))

@ref ITO s 39B(a), the lines marked as a temporary provision; fork F2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of the temporary provision of section 39B`
`section 39B — the reading row IL-27 takes of the temporary provision` MEANS
    `declined where the readings differ`

@ref ITO s 39B(a), the lines marked as a temporary provision; fork F2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 39B does not say how its temporary provision for tax years 2026 and 2027 relates to paragraphs (1) and (2), and here the readings differ` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 39B does not say how its temporary provision for tax years 2026 and 2027 relates to paragraphs (1) and (2), and here the readings differ"

@ref ITO s 39B, commencement not in the source bundle
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the commencement of section 39B is in an amending Law that is not in the source bundle, so a tax year before 2026 is not answered` MEANS
    REFUSE "the commencement of section 39B is in an amending Law that is not in the source bundle, so a tax year before 2026 is not answered"

§§ `The credit points for a tax year`

@ref ITO s 39B(a), lines 1620-1626; fork F2
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the days` IS A NUMBER
      t IS A `A reading of the temporary provision of section 39B`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 39B — the points in tax year` `the year` `for days of service` `the days` `, reading the temporary provision as` t MEANS
    IF   `the year` LESS THAN 2026
    THEN `the commencement of section 39B is in an amending Law that is not in the source bundle, so a tax year before 2026 is not answered`
    ELSE IF   `the year` GREATER THAN 2027
         THEN `s 39B(a)(1), (2) — the points for days of service` `the days`
         ELSE CONSIDER t
              WHEN `the temporary provision replaces paragraphs (1) and (2) in tax years 2026 and 2027`
                  THEN `s 39B(a) temporary provision — the points for days of service` `the days`
              WHEN `paragraphs (1) and (2) govern in every tax year`
                  THEN `s 39B(a)(1), (2) — the points for days of service` `the days`
              WHEN `declined where the readings differ`
                  THEN IF   `the days` LESS THAN 20
                       THEN 0
                       ELSE `section 39B does not say how its temporary provision for tax years 2026 and 2027 relates to paragraphs (1) and (2), and here the readings differ`

@ref ITO s 39B(a), lines 1620-1626; forks F1, F2
GIVEN t IS A `A reading of the temporary provision of section 39B`
      r IS A `A reading of the sections that name no residence condition (ss 39A, 39B, 40A, 40B)`
      i IS A `A combat reservist in a tax year, for section 39B`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 39B, reading the temporary provision as` t `and the residence condition as` r `, for` i MEANS
    `for tax year` (i's `tax year`) `, row IL-27 answers`
        (`the points, unless section 48A may take them from a foreign worker:` (i's `a foreign worker`) `,`
            (`points under a section that names no residence condition, for` (i's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`) `, the points being` `the points` `, reading the condition as` r))
    WHERE
        `the points` MEANS
            `s 39B — the points in tax year` (i's `tax year`) `for days of service` (i's `days of reserve service as a fighter in the previous tax year`) `, reading the temporary provision as` t

-- At the readings the two switches name: both declined where they decide.
@export The credit points under Income Tax Ordinance s 39B (reserve service as a fighter) for a tax year from 2026: three quarters of a point for 20 days or more in the previous tax year and a quarter more for each further five days, to 4, under paragraphs (1) and (2) or the temporary provision for 2026 and 2027; declines where those readings differ, for one who is not an Israeli resident, and for a foreign worker (s 48A)
@ref ITO s 39B, lines 1620-1629
GIVEN i IS A `A combat reservist in a tax year, for section 39B`
          @desc the tax year, residence, and the days of reserve service as a fighter in the previous tax year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 39B for` i MEANS
    `the credit points under section 39B, reading the temporary provision as` `section 39B — the reading row IL-27 takes of the temporary provision` `and the residence condition as` `the reading row IL-27 takes of the sections that name no residence condition` `, for` i

@ref ITO s 39B, s 33A
GIVEN i IS A `A combat reservist in a tax year, for section 39B`
      `the value of one credit point` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit under section 39B, in NIS, for` i `, at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` MEANS
    `the credit points under section 39B for` i TIMES `the value of one credit point`
